==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|de}} {{term|race|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|it|de}} {{term|razza|lang=it}}, possibly from {{etyl|ar|de}} {{term|sc=Arab|رأس|رأس|tr=ra’s|lang=ar|head}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=f|plural=Rassen}}

# [[race]] (human, horse, ...)
# [[Nazi]] term to distinguish between a part of the population considered "pure" "[[Aryan]]" and others
# (''Rasse haben''):
#: ''Die Frau hat Rasse''

